      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "There are several common reasons why just one room in your rental property might not be getting enough cool air. One possibility is that the room is located on the opposite side of the house from the air handler, resulting in increased resistance to airflow. Another potential cause is an obstruction, such as a piece of furniture or a wall, blocking the path of the cooled air. Additionally, issues with the ductwork, like a clogged or restricted vent, can also prevent cooled air from reaching the desired room. It's worth inspecting the duct system in that room for any blockages or restrictions.",
